al Takeaways (2021–2024 Cycle) ; Television Broadcast Rights: $3.25 billion; TOP Programme Sponsorship: $871.5 million ; Organizing ...\",\"url\":\"https://swimswam.com/the-iocs-olympic-billions-and-swimmings-piece-of-the-pie-financial-report/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"117\",\"title\":\"IOC lose another worldwide sponsor as Intel departure confirmed\",\"description\":\"Jun 18, 2025 · From fractionally over $1 billion in the 2013-2016 quadrennium, TOP programme revenues more than doubled to nearly $2.3 billion in the cycle ...\",\"url\":\"https://duncanmackayveritas.substack.com/p/exclusive-ioc-lose-another-worldwide\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"118\",\"title\":\"IOC and Allianz extend Olympic TOP sponsorship ahead ... - SportsPro\",\"description\":\"Mar 13, 2025 · The IOC recorded revenue of US$7.6 billion for the cycle ending with the 2021 Tokyo Games, with TOP contributing about 30 per cent, which made ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.sportspro.com/news/ioc-allianz-olympics-top-sponsor-march-2025/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"119\",\"title\":\"Winter Olympics: The sponsors and partners at a glance - ISPO.com\",\"description\":\"Jun 23, 2025 · For the current Olympic cycle from 2025 to 2028, 7.3 billion US dollars in revenue was already secured at the end of 2024 according to IOC ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.ispo.com/en/sports-business/winter-olympics-sponsors-and-partners\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"120\",\"title\":\"The Economics of Hosting the Olympic Games\",\"description\":\"The IOC requires cities hosting the summer games to have a minimum of forty thousand available hotel rooms, which in Rio's case necessitated the ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.cfr.org/backgrounder/economics-hosting-olympic-games\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"121\",\"title\":\"What are the true costs of hosting the Olympics? | LGT\",\"description\":\"Aug 8, 2024 · Firstly, cities invest millions – somewhere between $50 to $100 million – in evaluating, preparing and submitting a bid to the IOC.2 Once a city ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.lgtwm.com/uk-en/insights/market-views/what-are-the-true-costs-of-hosting-the-olympics-228636\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"122\",\"title\":\"Time to scrap the Olympics? | Saïd Business School\",\"description\":\"Sep 7, 2020 · Our study has established that all Olympic Games experienced high cost overrun, averaging 172%. Our new findings suggest that for the Games, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.sbs.ox.ac.uk/oxford-answers/time-scrap-olympics\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"123\",\"title\":\"The Oxford Olympics Study 2016: Cost and Cost Overrun at the Games\",\"description\":\"Jul 5, 2016 · Main findings of the study are, first, that average actual out turn cost for Summer Games is USD 5.2 billion (2015 level), and USD 3.1 billion for Winter Games.\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=2804554\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"124\",\"title\":\"The 40-year hangover: how the 1976 Olympics nearly broke Montreal\",\"description\":\"Jul 6, 2016 · The Montreal Olympics left the city with a C$1.6bn debt, a string of corruption scandals, and a creeping sense of economic and social decline.\",\"url\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/cities/2016/jul/06/40-year-hangover-1976-olympic-games-broke-montreal-canada\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"125\",\"title\":\"1976 Montreal Olympics: Case Study of Project Management Failure\",\"description\":\"Although the original cost estimate for the facilities was $120 million, the final cost was $1.5 billion, with $830 million for the main stadium alone. Part of ...\",\"url\":\"https://engagedscholarship.csuohio.edu/encee_facpub/21/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"126\",\"title\":\"Athens 2004, the squandered legacy - InsideTheGames\",\"description\":\"Mar 23, 2024 · According to the Greek finance ministry, the Athens Olympics cost 8.5 billion euros, a staggering figure given the economic crisis that has hit ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.insidethegames.biz/articles/1144355/athens-2004-the-squandered-legacy\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"127\",\"title\":\"How the Olympics rotted Greece - Politico.eu\",\"description\":\"Jul 10, 2015 · Other estimates put the cost of the Athens Games at more than €7 billion, perhaps a lot more. Those figures may include upgrades to hospitals ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.politico.eu/article/how-the-olympics-rotted-greece/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"128\",\"title\":\"Los Angeles 1984 Olympic Games - Britannica\",\"description\":\"The Olympics turned a profit ($225 million) for the first time since 1932. Despite concerns about growing corporate involvement and the reduced competition ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/event/Los-Angeles-1984-Olympic-Games\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"129\",\"title\":\"The Money Pit That Is Montreal's Olympic Stadium | The Walrus\",\"description\":\"Mar 25, 2024 · The name refers to the hundreds of millions of dollars the vexed landmark has cost the province over the past three decades—to construct it, ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://thewalrus.ca/montreal-olympic-stadium/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"130\",\"title\":\"Indebted Greeks Question the Cost of the 2004 Olympics | TIME.com\",\"description\":\"Jul 9, 2012 · Eight years after the Athens Summer Games, Greece is in economic turmoil, and the value of all the expensive facilities is in question.\",\"url\":\"https://olympics.time.com/2012/07/09/amid-economic-turmoil-some-greeks-look-back-at-2004-olympics-as-losing-proposition/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"131\",\"title\":\"Olympic cities can become multi-billion-dollar graveyards for white ...\",\"description\":\"Aug 6, 2021 · Olympic cities can become multi-billion-dollar graveyards for white elephants after the Games · A snow covered Olympic stadium · The Rio Olympics ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.abc.net.au/news/2021-08-07/what-japan-learned-from-olympic-white-elephants/100329488\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"132\",\"title\":\"The Economic Impact of Hosting the Olympics - Investopedia\",\"description\":\"Hosting the Olympics tends to result in severe economic deficiencies for cities. Unless a city already has the existing infrastructure to support the excess ...Costs of Hosting the Olympics · Examples of Olympics Cost\",\"url\":\"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/markets-economy/092416/what-economic-impact-hosting-olympics.asp\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"133\",\"title\":\"Paris 2024: A Less Expensive Games? | by Bent Flyvbjerg - Medium\",\"description\":\"Jun 28, 2024 · With a cost of USD 8.7 billion and a cost overrun of 115%, is Paris 2024 living up to IOC policy for a cheaper Games, so more cities will want ...\",\"url\":\"https://bentflyvbjerg.medium.com/paris-2024-a-less-expensive-games-f0757cf825d9\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"134\",\"title\":\"The Oxford Olympics Study 2024: Are Cost and Cost Overrun ... - arXiv\",\"description\":\"Jun 3, 2024 · We document that the Games remain costly and continue to have large cost overruns, to a degree that threatens their viability.\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.01714\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"135\",\"title\":\"Olympic rings - Symbol of the Olympic Movement\",\"description\":\"Created by Pierre de Coubertin, the Olympic symbol consists of five interlaced rings of equal dimensions that represent the union of the five continents and ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.olympics.com/ioc/olympic-rings\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"136\",\"title\":\"Who created the Olympic rings symbol?\",\"description\":\"The Rings appeared for the first time in 1913 at the top of a letter written by Pierre de Coubertin, the founder of the modern Olympic Games.\",\"url\":\"https://www.olympics.com/ioc/faq/olympic-symbol-and-identity/who-created-the-olympic-rings-symbol\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"137\",\"title\":\"Olympic flag - Symbol of the Olympic Movement\",\"description\":\"The interlocking rings were first drawn by Pierre de Coubertin – the founder of the modern Olympic Games – on a letter in July 1913. Soon after, the rings made ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.olympics.com/ioc/olympic-flag\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"138\",\"title\":\"Olympic Properties\",\"description\":\"The Olympic Properties refer to the Olympic symbol, flag, motto, anthem, identifications and any musical, audio-visual or creative works created in ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.olympics.com/ioc/olympic-properties\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"139\",\"title\":\"The Olympic motto\",\"description\":\"Jul 20, 2021 · The original Olympic motto \\\"Citius, Altius, Fortius\\\" was adopted with the launch of the Olympic Movement in 1894 at the urging of founder ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.olympics.com/ioc/olympic-motto\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"140\",\"title\":\"“Faster, Higher, Stronger - Together” - IOC Session approves historic ...\",\"description\":\"Jul 20, 2021 · The change adds the word “together” after an en dash to “Faster, Higher, Stronger”. The new Olympic motto now reads: “Faster, Higher, Stronger – ...Missing:  history | Show results with:history\",\"url\":\"https://olympics.com/ioc/news/-faster-higher-stronger-together-ioc-session-approves-historic-change-in-olympic-motto\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"141\",\"title\":\"The History of the Olympic Flame\",\"description\":\"Oct 24, 2017 · That decision coincided with the creation of the Olympic Torch Relay – the brainchild of the university lecturer and sports theorist Carl Diem.\",\"url\":\"https://olympics.com/ioc/news/the-history-of-the-olympic-flame\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"142\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Factsheet: The Olympic Torch Relay\",\"description\":\"Jul 9, 2021 · Inspired by torch races that were held in ancient Greek times, Diem suggested that for the 1936 Summer Games a Flame be lit in Olympia and ...\",\"url\":\"https://stillmed.olympics.com/media/Documents/Olympic-Games/Factsheets/The-Olympic-torch-relay.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"143\",\"title\":\"Olympic Torch Relay - History, Highlights \u0026 Torch Bearers\",\"description\":\"A modern invention inspired by practices from ancient Greece, the Olympic Torch Relay heralds the start of the Olympic Games and transmits a message of peace ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.olympics.com/en/olympic-games/olympic-torch-relay\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"144\",\"title\":\"How do the Olympic Games opening and closing ceremonies take ...\",\"description\":\"Today, Rule 55 of the Olympic Charter specifies some of the protocol that has to be followed during the ceremonies and the words used by the head of state of ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.olympics.com/ioc/faq/games-ceremonies-and-protocol/how-do-the-olympic-games-opening-and-closing-ceremonies-take-place\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"145\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Opening Ceremony of the Games of the Olympiad - Olympics.com\",\"description\":\"Page 1. •. •. •. •. •. •. •. •. •. •. •. •. •. •. •. Page 2. Page 3. Page 4. Page 5. Page 6. Page 7.\",\"url\":\"https://stillmed.olympics.com/media/Documents/Olympic-Games/Factsheets/The-opening-ceremony-of-the-Games-of-the-Olympiad.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"146\",\"title\":\"What is the Olympic oath and when was it created?\",\"description\":\"The Olympic oath is one of the protocol elements of the Opening Ceremony. It is taken by an athlete from the host county, on behalf of all the athletes.\",\"url\":\"https://www.olympics.com/ioc/faq/games-ceremonies-and-protocol/what-is-the-olympic-oath-and-when-was-it-created\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"147\",\"title\":\"The history of spectacular Olympic opening ceremonies | PBS News\",\"description\":\"Jul 26, 2024 · At the first modern Olympics in 1896, in Athens, athletes simply entered the stadium to hear speeches and a specially composed hymn – though ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/the-history-of-spectacular-olympic-opening-ceremonies\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"148\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The closing ceremony of the Olympic Games\",\"description\":\"Page 1. Page 2. Page 3.\",\"url\":\"https://stillmed.olympics.com/media/Documents/Olympic-Games/Factsheets/The-closing-ceremony-of-the-Olympic-Games.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"149\",\"title\":\"All About Closing Ceremony at Paris Olympics 2024 - NBC\",\"description\":\"Aug 11, 2024 · For starters, the Closing Ceremony begins with the Parade of Flags, in which athletes from each nation walk with their flag into the stadium.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nbc.com/nbc-insider/all-about-closing-ceremony-paris-olympics-2024-how-to-watch\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"150\",\"title\":\"10 Iconic Olympic Games Opening and Closing Ceremonies\",\"description\":\"Jun 21, 2024 · Paris 1924 marked the first official Closing Ceremony and included the now traditional flag raising of the International Olympic Committee, host ...\",\"url\":\"https://blog.imago-images.com/en/olympics-ceremonies\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"151\",\"title\":\"Opening and Closing Olympic Ceremonies - John Ed Mathison\",\"description\":\"Aug 7, 2025 · This tradition started in 1956 at the Melbourne Games. You might remember that high political tensions had caused several countries not to ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://johnedmathison.org/opening-and-closing-olympic-ceremonies/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"152\",\"title\":\"New traditions - Olympics.com\",\"description\":\"Feb 28, 2025 · It involves the top three athletes or teams in each event taking their places on a podium. The third-placed athlete or team stands to the left ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.olympics.com/en/news/new-traditions\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"153\",\"title\":\"Games, Ceremonies and Protocol - FAQ - Olympics.com\",\"description\":\"The FAQ covers the role of the IOC, who organizes the games, the role of a country's government, how ceremonies take place, the Olympic oath, and why athletes ...Missing:  rules | Show results with:rules\",\"url\":\"https://www.olympics.com/ioc/faq/games-ceremonies-and-protocol\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"154\",\"title\":\"The Olympic podium is born\",\"description\":\"Feb 28, 2025 · IOC President Count Henri de Baillet-Latour, who presented the medals at the 1932 inaugural medal ceremony, got the idea for the Olympic podium ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.olympics.com/en/news/the-olympic-podium-is-born\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"155\",\"title\":\"Olympic Ceremonies - Olympedia\",\"description\":\"This ceremony was adopted in 1932; earlier all medals were handed out at the end of the Games, usually by the head of state of the host nation. Did you know?\",\"url\":\"https://www.olympedia.org/definitions/113\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"156\",\"title\":\"What is the protocol for awarding medals when multiple athletes tie ...\",\"description\":\"Jul 16, 2024 · If there is a tie for first, there are two gold medals, no silver, and one bronze. If there is a tie for second, there is one gold, two silver, and no bronze.When Olympic athletes share a gold medal after they both win in a ...Can you explain the differences between gold, silver, and bronze ...More results from www.quora.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.quora.com/What-is-the-protocol-for-awarding-medals-when-multiple-athletes-tie-in-a-competition\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"157\",\"title\":\"[PDF] IF Opening and Closing Ceremony Award ... - The World Games\",\"description\":\"At least two high-ranking officials (preferably more in the case of team sports) will be required for the ceremonies, at least one of whom should be from the IF ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.theworldgames.org/files/Governing_Documents/IF%2520Opening%2C%2520Closing%2520\u0026%2520Medal%2520Ceremonies%2520-%2520Specifics%2520\u0026%2520Protocols.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"158\",\"title\":\"I.O.C. Modifies Its Mask Mandate for Medals Ceremony\",\"description\":\"Jul 31, 2021 · Only after a signal from an Olympic official will the medalist