le\":\"The history of the summer olympic games | Sports Medicine News\",\"description\":\"The first Modern Olympic Games were hosted in the Panathenaic Stadium in Athens in 1896. 241 athletes from 14 different Nations competed in 43 events.\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.sportsmed.org/membership/sports-medicine-update/summer-2024/history-of-olympic-sport\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"243\",\"title\":\"How many athletes and countries participate in the Olympics? A ...\",\"description\":\"Jul 29, 2024 · Around 11,000 athletes participated in the 2020 Tokyo Olympic Games, including 613 athletes from Team USA, according to the Olympics website. ...\",\"url\":\"https://sports.yahoo.com/many-athletes-countries-participate-olympics-071828459.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"244\",\"title\":\"Olympic Participation Trends: Insights into Games and it's Impact\",\"description\":\"Apr 12, 2024 · Regional Representation: Historically, European nations dominated participation. However, recent decades have witnessed a surge in participation ...\",\"url\":\"https://businessanalyticsinstitute.com/olympic-participation-trends-analysis/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"245\",\"title\":\"IOC Refugee Olympic Team\",\"description\":\"Created in 2015, consisting of 10 athletes, the Refugee Olympic Team competed for the first time at the Rio 2016 games, inspiring the world with strength ...Olympic News · Refugee Olympic Team · Rio 2016 Refugee Olympic... · Tokyo 2020\",\"url\":\"https://www.olympics.com/ioc/refugee-olympic-team\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"246\",\"title\":\"Largest-ever Refugee Olympic Team makes its entrance as Paris ...\",\"description\":\"Jul 30, 2024 · The 37-strong team will compete across 12 sports, each having beaten extraordinary odds to take their place at the world's largest and most prestigious ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.unrefugees.org/news/largest-ever-refugee-olympic-team-makes-its-entrance-as-paris-games-open/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"247\",\"title\":\"Which countries have won the most medals at the Summer Olympics ...\",\"description\":\"Jul 18, 2024 · The United States leads the way with 2,643 total medals, 1,521 more than any other nation. The Soviet Union is in second place with 1,122 medals ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nbcolympics.com/news/which-countries-have-won-most-medals-summer-olympics-updating-tally-paris-2024\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"248\",\"title\":\"Which country has the most Summer Olympic gold medals of all-time?\",\"description\":\"Aug 11, 2024 · Here's a look at the top 10 countries in the all-time Summer Olympics gold medal count: United States - 1,061; Soviet Union - 395; Great ...\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.nbcchicago.com/paris-2024-summer-olympics/after-2024-paris-games-which-country-has-the-most-summer-olympic-gold-medals-of-all-time/3519470/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"249\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://www.statista.com/chart/32725/the-nations-with-most-summer-olympic-medals/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"250\",\"title\":\"A Visual History of Which Countries Have Dominated the Summer ...\",\"description\":\"the United States, Australia and eight European nations — earned medals in the first modern Games, in Athens in 1896.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2016/08/08/sports/olympics/history-olympic-dominance-charts.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"251\",\"title\":\"Data visualization analyzes the East vs West rivalry at the Olympics\",\"description\":\"Conversely, the Soviet Union didn't win any Gold medals until the 1952 Summer Games, with China not registering an Olympic triumph until 1984. However, both ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.yellowfinbi.com/blog/data-visualization-analyzes-the-east-vs-west-rivalry-at-the-olympics\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"252\",\"title\":\"Olympic Medals by Country 2025 - World Population Review\",\"description\":\"Former countries that had the most Olympic medals are: Soviet Union (1204), East Germany (519), West Germany (243), Czechoslovakia (171) and Yugoslavia (87).\",\"url\":\"https://worldpopulationreview.com/country-rankings/olympic-medals-by-country\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"253\",\"title\":\"Countries with the most Summer Olympic gold medals of all time\",\"description\":\"Aug 12, 2024 · Tied for gold: US, China make history knotted at 40 top prizes each · United States: 1,110 · Soviet Union: 395 · Great Britain: 306 · People's ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nbcdfw.com/paris-2024-summer-olympics/countries-most-summer-olympic-gold-medals-all-time/3619130/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"254\",\"title\":\"What Determines Countries' Olympic Success? - Econofact\",\"description\":\"Jul 17, 2024 · The success of individual Olympic athletes reflects many factors including raw talent, dedication, training, effort, experience, and even luck.\",\"url\":\"https://econofact.org/what-determines-countries-olympic-success\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"255\",\"title\":\"Olympic medals and demo-economic factors: Novel predictors, the ...\",\"description\":\"Winning Olympic medals depends on the combined potential of population, wealth, growth rate, unemployment, ex-host, and social-sport expenditures.\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1441352311000489\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"256\",\"title\":\"How economics impact Olympic achievement - Marketplace.org\",\"description\":\"Aug 1, 2024 · How economics impact Olympic achievement. A country's athletic infrastructure as well as subsidies and citizens' health influence medal counts.\",\"url\":\"https://www.marketplace.org/story/2024/08/01/economy-olympics-economic-sports-subsidized-medals\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"257\",\"title\":\"The Massive Costs Behind The Olympic Games [Infographic] - Forbes\",\"description\":\"Jul 21, 2021 · In more recent years, the 2016 Olympics in Rio de Janeiro cost just under $14 billion which represented a 352% cost overrun while the 2012 Games ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/niallmccarthy/2021/07/21/the-massive-costs-behind-the-olympic-games-infographic/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"258\",\"title\":\"10 Olympic Games That Nearly Bankrupted Their Host Countries\",\"description\":\"These Olympics were budgeted at a modest CA$120 million (U.S. $110 million), but construction overruns resulted in a CA$922 million deficit that overwhelmed ...\",\"url\":\"https://entertainment.howstuffworks.com/10-olympic-games-bankrupted-host-countries.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"259\",\"title\":\"The Price of Glory: Costs and Benefits of Olympic Hosting | Beirne\",\"description\":\"Jul 18, 2024 · Hosting costs include infrastructure, sports facilities, and ceremonies. Benefits include tourism and legacy, but costs often overrun budgets, ...Missing:  fiscal | Show results with:fiscal\",\"url\":\"https://www.beirnegroup.com/blog/price-glory-costs-and-benefits-olympic-hosting\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"260\",\"title\":\"The True Cost of Olympic Glory: An Economic Perspective | Vantage\",\"description\":\"Rio 2016: The Rio Olympics had an initial operational budget of $2.7 billion but ended up with a total expenditure of around $13.2 billion. The city made ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.vantagemarkets.com/academy/olympics-cost/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"261\",\"title\":\"The causal economic effects of Olympic Games on host regions\",\"description\":\"This paper is the first to study the effects of hosting Olympic Games on regional economic output beyond population dynamics.\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0166046221000338\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"262\",\"title\":\"Is Hosting the Olympic Games Worth It? | Poole Thought Leadership\",\"description\":\"Jul 24, 2024 · The IOC claims the event creates jobs and boosts tourism and leaves behind facilities that provide lasting benefits to the community.Missing:  empirical | Show results with:empirical\",\"url\":\"https://poole.ncsu.edu/thought-leadership/article/is-hosting-the-olympic-games-worth-it/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"263\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Olympic Effect Andrew K. Rose Mark M. Spiegel Working Paper ...\",\"description\":\"Our empirical results show that the Olympic effect is robust; hosting the games tends to increase a country's openness substantively and permanently. But ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w14854/w14854.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"264\",\"title\":\"Olympic transformation of metropolitan cities—for better or for worse\",\"description\":\"Aug 29, 2024 · For the 1996 Atlanta Olympics, almost 30,000 Atlantans were uprooted from their homes and faced challenges in finding affordable housing, and ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.brookings.edu/articles/olympic-transformation-of-metropolitan-cities-for-better-or-for-worse/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"265\",\"title\":\"7 Ways Hosting the Olympics Impacts a City | Britannica\",\"description\":\"The sought-after positive legacy outcomes include urban renewal, increased tourism and employment, enhanced city image and reputation, improved public welfare, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/list/7-ways-hosting-the-olympics-impacts-a-city\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"266\",\"title\":\"History of the Olympics: Promoting Cultural Acceptance - YFU USA\",\"description\":\"Jul 26, 2024 · Athletes, coaches, and spectators from around the world converge in the host city, creating a melting pot of languages, traditions, and customs.\",\"url\":\"https://yfuusa.org/2024/07/26/history-of-the-olympics-promoting-cultural-acceptance/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"267\",\"title\":\"Olympic effects on reshaping urban greenspace of host cities\",\"description\":\"Results show that Olympic Games not only promote overall increases in greenspace coverage but also enhance people's ambient exposure to greenspace.\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S016920462200264X\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"268\",\"title\":\"5 Reasons Why the Olympics Are Important\",\"description\":\"Aug 1, 2024 · The Olympics bring together athletes and spectators from around the world to a single host city, creating a melting pot of languages, traditions ...\",\"url\":\"https://cnr.ncsu.edu/news/2024/08/why-the-olympics-are-important/\",\"favicon\":\"\"}],\"images\":[{\"id\":\"22aa3769deef\",\"caption\":\"Olympic Rings\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Olympic_rings_without_rims.svg.png\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"615dfb50f6df\",\"caption\":\"Baron Pierre de Coubertin\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Baron_Pierre_de_Coubertin.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"2f96492b9a36\",\"caption\":\"Ruins of the ancient stadium at Olympia\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Olympia-stadion.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"2f96492b9a36\",\"caption\":\"Ancient Olympic Stadium\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Olympia-stadion.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"2f96492b9a36\",\"caption\":\"Archaeological remains at Olympia\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Olympia-stadion.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"9dab922bd255\",\"caption\":\"Evangelos Zappas\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Evangelos_Zappas.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"615dfb50f6df\",\"caption\":\"Baron Pierre de Coubertin\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Baron_Pierre_de_Coubertin.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"4cc26fc6797c\",\"caption\":\"Opening ceremony of the 1896 Olympic Games\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/1896_Olympic_opening_ceremony.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"3cba1ff9d46a\",\"caption\":\"Francis Field during 1904 Olympics\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Francis_Field_1904.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"22aa3769deef\",\"caption\":\"Olympic Rings\",\"url\":\".